    {
      "id": "action",
      "instance": "d19f825e-c4ee-492a-8eb5-c0cad8b2293f",
      "properties": [
        [
          "name",
          "LSASS Memory Credential Dumping"
        ],
        [
          "tactic_id",
          "TA0006"
        ],
        [
          "tactic_ref",
          "x-mitre-tactic--2558fd61-8c75-4730-900d-122e8cdaea9e"
        ],
        [
          "technique_id",
          "T1003.001"
        ],
        [
          "technique_ref",
          "attack-pattern--65f2d882-3f41-4d48-8a06-29af77ec9f90"
        ],
        [
          "description",
          "Once on an internal Windows host with local admin rights (or after a privilege escalation), the attacker uses tools such as Mimikatz or a custom LSASS dump technique to extract NTLM hashes and Kerberos tickets from memory. This yields credentials for additional domain accounts, including potentially privileged service accounts."
        ],
        [
          "confidence",
          "reported"
        ],
        [
          "execution_start",
          null
        ],
        [
          "execution_end",
          null
        ],
